 things that uh the  game of golf has never seen before  when you talk to people about live  they suggest that there's been a  violation of some kind of unspoken honor  code in golf or you're going to change  the culture  of golf and make it more vulgar  more populist  less honorable  i know you hear versions of that i'm not  sure i'm describing it exactly right but  the spirit of golf is being spirited  somehow  despoiled or desecrated by this how do  you respond to that  well a spirit of golf look i think  that in every industry no matter what it  is it's always been changing  innovating right and golf i don't think  is anything different  over the course of time if we want to  continue to grow the game or make the  game more interesting  if you're going to keep it with hickory  shafts and up a lot of ball and  you know no technology  people are not going to be interested by  that we've got to find ways to make it  more interesting whether it's  you know a new format  teams  that's personally one of my favorite  things about lip lip golf is the team  aspect no i think it's enhancing the  spirit of the game so pga tour is saying  that anyone who participates and live  will be banned for life from pga yeah it  doesn't matter 28 are you worried about  that no no i think it'll get figured out  and then i personally know that it will  get figured out whether it's legally or  whether they come to the table and work  out terms i definitely think it'll it'll  all wash itself out in the future uh  pretty shortly  um but it's funny it's it's so weird  because it's like  let's use this as a reference i heard  this earlier this week  you have a pizza shop that's been in  existence for 50 years and all the  customers go to it's a great product all  of a sudden a new pizza shop opens up  right and they start paying the  customers to come eat at their place and  that pizza is potentially a little bit  better of a of a pizza right  and then all of a sudden that original  pizza house goes if you go over there  we're banning you from member coming  back to our you know pizza shop what's  wrong with that economic model  that does seem short-sighted yeah  particularly if you have been the only  pizza shop in town if you've had a  monopoly correct that's probably not  allowed correct but there is this vibe  in golf it's more than a vibe it's a  kind of stated  ethic where you know it's not really  about the money or you should play for  free or  well in that case it just becomes a  hobby  yeah  we're playing for free i mean there's  our livelihoods and you know there's a  there's a great economic opportunity for  golfers to make a lot of money i mean  that's why we grew up playing golf also  for the history to go win majors and win  pga tour events initially and now i'm  out here i want to win live events i  mean you see the passion and competitive  aspect of this environment out here and  we all want to compete to win every  single week you know anytime anyone  invests over a billion dollars into  let's say the game of golf how is that  not going to grow the game how is that  not going to provide more opportunities  what is your parents your friends your  caddy you know  what did they all say well when we  looked at the economics it was solely  for the economics it was a no-brainer  considering the relationships i've built  with my sponsors considering  the relationship i have with the tour  the relationship i have with with uh my  competitors out there on tour as well i  had to think about all of that and how  that affected my livelihood moving  forward in the future and i had to wait  does the pros outweigh the cons and for  me from a financial perspective resource  allocation perspective meaning like i'm  able to do things now in dallas  and i think we can get to that in a  little bit  but i had to wait all those consequences  show a social consequence how i was  going to be viewed publicly i've got a  youtube channel now that's growing and  doing very well and want to continue to  produce product  there so i can showcase entertainment  and my skill set uh on that platform as  well you are well known for for bringing  science to golf yeah give us an example  wow well there's a lot of examples one  of them that i can think of directly off  the top of my head  this is more statistics but hitting it  farther has been a big notion of mine  and the reason i did that was because i  knew that if i could gain  three more yards off the tee  i could get i could be six more yards  offline so three more yards right or  left  and still  have a positive strokes gained  uh potential and what that means is that  i'm gaining shots on the field and so  from that perspective i took it on to me  how do i hit it farther how do i  consistently hit it farther how do i get  my body stronger what do i do from a  biomechanics perspective to make my golf  swing more repeatable so i'll go on  gears and try and understand how my  biomechanics are moving  in order to be the most repeatable and  powerful athlete i can possibly be so  how do you do that  a lot of studying data trying to  understand and crunching numbers start  trying to understand  how to create flat spots in the golf  swing this is getting really technical  now  please do okay uh trying to create flat  spots on the golf swing where you're  making a  combined motion that allows the golf  club to move in a very consistent  straight manner yeah it's not this  arcing manner that you're very sensitive  to air on you're trying to become less  sensitive to air so when i'm able to  like wrap around the corner this club is  going down  but because i'm going up it's actually  planing out and it goes straight into  the ball so your angle of attack's more  consistent you're lofted impact your  dynamic lofted impacts more consistent  so you're hitting  your spots a lot more consistently  meaning that your launch angle is going  to be consistent your spin rate's going  to be consistent and your landing  distance is going to be way more  consistent so you're doing calculations  in your head as you  yeah yeah we can't use uh green's books  which have a topographical map of the  putting green tells me exactly oh this  is 2.3 slope so we get i i know on  average what a 2 slope looks like a 3  slope looks like it's not me doing math  in my head i just have  memorized all the numbers do you count  cards in blackjack uh no i could but i  don't want to go down that route road i  don't want to get in trouble  that's totally fair but in golf you're  allowed to do this correct trying to  find a distinct advantage to help  benefit the game of golf in a positive  way and help my life out in the most in  the best way possible  amazing and as it paid off  well do you think it's paid off well it  sounds like it has i think it has for me  i'm very blessed i'm very lucky my  family's um very very happy  my friends around me are very happy i  know i'm now able to do things back in  dallas give back to my community in  dallas  building i'm going to build a  multi-sport complex center there attach  an education center there attach my  charity to it my charity bryson chamber  foundation supports junior golf health  and it's going to build an education  center i want to build an education  center without got an idea and model for  that i think will help benefit the  education system in general  so the resources that i now have doesn't  mean that i'm able to just sit on my  butt and and do nothing  i've got more responsibility now to take  care of my community my country  and my state  as much as i possibly can and at a  certain point in time you go man there's  more to life than just golf and that's  what live golf allows me to do i mean  i'm able to play golf and enjoy and  compete with some of the best players in  the world  but also have a life outside of this  subscribe to the fox news youtube  channel to catch our nightly opens  stories that are changing the